{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues","id":1445666,"title":"Running a Lunar, Solar, and DB campaign, any issues?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-24T08:01:41-07:00","id":1445666,"title":"Running a Lunar, Solar, and DB campaign, any issues?","content":"Hello all, I am going to be running a new 3rd edition campaign soon and multiple different types of Exalted are going to be in the game. So I was hoping you had any advice or warnings for issues you have experienced running mixed campaigns? I am a long time ST &amp; player for Exalted, all the way back to the 1st edition of the game, so I understand there have been major balance issues in the past, but I have been told that the narrowing of the power differences have alleviated this quite a bit. So I assume the biggest issues will be the themes of the different games and motivations of the characters that I need to be most aware of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T09:26:50-07:00","id":1445676,"title":"","content":"I think Lunars and Solars will work together pretty well, just as long as the Lunar players don't try to compete with the specific niches of the Solars (basically, what the Solars are Supernal in). A Lunar wanting to be a great crafter is pretty much going to be overshadowed if there's also a Solar with Supernal Craft. Note, though, that some areas are a lot broader than others, and have much more room for multiple people to be good at them. Combat is a good example here. While a Lunar shouldn't expect to make &quot;the greatest sword-master in the world&quot; work alongside a Melee-Supernal Dawn, they can still be extremely effective in combat overall, and contribute meaningfully. This is particularly true because Lunar charms tend to be applicable to multiple types of fighting, making the Lunars more versatile. As the most basic example, the Lunar Dexterity Excellency can be added to any attack, pretty much, meaning that the Lunar can be pretty good at fighting armed or unarmed, and with bows, thrown knives, or just rocks, in a way that a Solar might struggle to match.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded, however, are a bit more dicey. While the power differential has definitely been <i>lowered</i> in 3e, with no bullshit &quot;this charm completely fails against a Celestial Exalt&quot; mechanics, the DB charms are still notably weaker than Lunar, and <i>especially</i> Solar ones. A DB in a party of Lunars/Solars runs a real risk of feeling useless. Some suggestions to compensate for this:<ul><li>First, the most RAW approach is to make sure the DBs' unique status as the most &quot;legitimate&quot; type of Exalts in Creation is emphasized. Encourage DBs to take &quot;social&quot; merits like Command, Backing, Influence, etc. at character creation, and in play, be a bit more lenient about giving them those merits as story awards. Also, they should run into far more people with positive Intimacies towards DBs in general, and less suspicion from the populace. They're the Princes of the Earth, saviors of Creation. Make sure that comes through.</li> <li>Starting any DBs at higher Essence is also a decent idea, allowing them to spend the XP they would have needed to reach the Essence level on whatever they want. I suggest Essence 3 for this, as it lets them take Signature charms, which are some of the really nice &quot;toys&quot; in the DB charmset.</li> <li>Straying further from the RAW, but adjusting the XP requirements for gaining higher Essence for the DBs is also a good idea. Right now, they &quot;plateau&quot; for a long time at Essence 3. Even if you gave them the 75 XP needed to start at Essence 3, as above, they'd still only be hitting Essence 4 after 175 XP, only 25 XP before the Solars and Lunars were hitting Essence 4 (i.e., about 5 sessions). If you give everybody the Solar/Lunar XP progression, on the other hand, then the DBs would be hitting Essence 4 at 125 XP, exactly when the Lunars and Solars are hitting Essence 3.</li> <li>Another idea, if you're not willing to start DBs at Essence 3, is to allow them access to one Signature charm in an Aspect Ability at Essence 2, a sort of &quot;mini-Supernal&quot; thing. Even if you start them at Essence 3, giving access to multiple Signature charms in a single Aspect Ability, again as a kind of mini-Supernal, isn't a bad idea. Normally, a DB can only take one Signature charm in an Ability, until they hit Essence 5, at which point they get a second. If in the one focus Ability, they can take, say, 2 Signature charms at Essence 3, 3 at Essence 4, and 4 at Essence 5, that's a nice little treat.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T16:24:24-07:00","id":1445728,"title":"","content":"We are playing a mixed Lunars/Solar campaign. But one Solar poses as DB within the satrapie of Prasad (well my version of Prasad that was written before the official material was written) and limits himself to stuff that would be expected from a DB.<br /> The other player is a Anathema that was indoctrinated through the Pure Way and they happen to became buddies.<br /> <br /> The Lunar is a freshly exalted Lunar comming into this group hiding/living in Prasad. She started at Essence 1 while everyone was almost E4. She was a player new to Exalted so we decided to go with 10xp/session while the others get 2/session so that she will catch up soon enough while learning the system. Besides this danger of being overwhelmed (that high XP DB start characters would also run into) from all the charms there are absolutely no problems. She chose a focus the others don't have and won't be going for. As long as the niche is protected even an E1 Lunar in an E4 Solar group does not feel off or weak. So the same should be true for Dragonblooded, I guess. I neither played or gm'ed a game for a DB yet so I can't really comment on that.<br /> <br /> Though as I said, one of my players poses as a Dragonblood. And he is smart in doing it, limiting demonstrations of his supernatural prowess for when it's necessary. That also means that many of his skills are not usable in certain situations. Like Kelly Pedersen already mentioned the social structure and capital a DB has can be incredible useful. Less so in stories where raw individual power is wanted but in a city setting (most of our time is spent in Kamthahar) it's incredible powerful.<br /> <br /> Sometimes even frustratingly so. The other player plays a Solar that &quot;just&quot; lives there and plays the role of a mortal sorceress. The &quot;DB&quot; player can leverage a lot of soft power over the other players if they don't want to behave in ways that garner unwanted attention. At least if it is public.<br /> <br /> <br /> In addition I don't know how you handle artifacts at your table but in my stories they are quite rare and powerful. From Solar PCs I always expect a very good reason and story about how they got their hands on those. Most of the time this already means that they don't take the artifact since they only want the +1 weapon that looks cool instead of the god-shaped creation that can potentially doom or create several kingdoms if it existence and carrier's name becomes known. DB can have heirlooms and more importantly they don't really care that they are known as carrier of an artifact. And in my opinion a DB carrying the Almighty Stick of Benefection or the Terrifying Bludgeon of Dragons has a way easier time creating and maintaining his reputation.<br /> <br /> In comparison a non-DB that becomes a carrier of a mighty artifact becomes target of other greedy entities and the Wyld Hunt. It is easier to hunt down a single individual without any support that might be very mighty or hunt down a known actor of an incredible powerful empire that would absolutely go to war with several legions lead by gods to reaquire the stolen artifact.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My (mostly) German Exalted blog: <a href=\"http://ryokiseck.de/\" target=\"_blank\">Praise the Spiral!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11185-ryoki","name":"Ryoki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T16:43:41-07:00","id":1445737,"title":"","content":"I'd say be mindful of the dice cap. If an enemy (Ahlat, Octavian) can add what is essentially +10 dice on a roll then the Lunars and Solars can match that. The DB can only add 6. It is very difficult for the Dragonblooded to match this.<br /> <br /> A quick fix to the issue is to make a Dragonblooded's dicecap (Ability + [Essence/2, round up]). This caps out at 8 dice, which is a lot better.<br /> <br /> I'll echo what Kelly said as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T17:37:31-07:00","id":1445750,"title":"","content":"The balance between the party members is actually a lot more dependent on how the players build their characters rather than their splat.<br /> <br /> If you look at the only currently published adventure for Exalted 3e, it's got a sample circle. You might have somebody who builds their Dawn Solar like that Dawn is built. You might also have a DB who's the party's sorcerer, who's stacking the Mela's Coil, a 5-dot jade daiklave, the spell Invulnerable Skin of Bronze, and optimized combat stats. In that case the guy who's supposed to be the sorcerer of the group, and also who's the DB of the group, will make the guy who built the Dawn look like a chump, <i>in addition</i> to being an awesome sorcerer.<br /> <br /> By far the biggest balance concern is not splat, it's how they're being built.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the total flip side, if each character has their niche and you do a good job as an ST, most of that won't even matter anyway. In Exalted people who are good at talking are extremely dangerous, sailing a ship is extremely dangerous, there's horrible magical diseases, soul extinguishing poisons, deadly environments, and massive labyrinthine bureaucracies of supernaturally mythic proportions.<br /> <br /> If your Dawn caste Solar is three times the warrior that the Dragonblooded doctor is, that's fine, because in the next scene when the Dawn is on the verge of literally* puking their guts out due to a magical virus that he can't just apply his daiklave to, it doesn't really matter that the terrestrial isn't as good a doctor as he could be if he was a Solar. There is no direct balance comparison here. The Dawn is only going to live to see another sunrise, ironically, because this Dragonblood was there and can cure their black-stomach fever.<br /> <br /> That's really on you though, if there's a DB doctor, absolutely put in that kind of disease that will straight up 100% end that Dawns life, and give him a chance to be saved the way he saves everyone in a fight.<br /> <br /> <br /> *I am using this word correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T04:28:58-07:00","id":1445951,"title":"","content":"I'm currently running a campaign in the South (blowing up Gem is always fun) with a Solar, a Lunar and two Dragon-Blooded. The Solar is a Bureaucracy supernal merchant, the Lunar is a Casteless sneaky-boy/jack of all trades, one of the Dragon-Blooded is a Wood Aspect desert warlord and the other is an Air Aspect demon-worshiping sorceress. The only adjustment I made was giving the Terrestrials a single free signature charm they otherwise qualify for at the start, that way they don't have to wait an eternity to get their fun toys. First player took the Water War fog charm and the other took Persistent Hornet Attack.<br /> The Celestials just hit Essence 2 last session and so far we haven't had any balance issues, since they all have distinct niches and are good at working together. Combat-wise the Solar is the least invested, which probably helps, he's a Laughing Monster practitioner good at kiting, the Lunar mostly tanks but can fill any role in a pinch through animal forms, and the Dragon-Blooded are both ranged fighters, using firewands and lightning bolts respectively. The fact that they use Martial Arts and Sorcery moreso than native Dragon-Blooded charms might have something to do with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":10131,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","user":"BadassOverlord","date":". 04-26-2021, 07:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T17:12:25-07:00","id":1446193,"title":"","content":"Basically, if there do end up being any DBs there needs to be VERY little overlap between their primary areas of expertise and those of the Celestials because anywhere there is overlap the DBs will be adding little in relative terms.<br /> <br /> In scenarios where everyone will or might be contributing in similar ways (e.g.- combat, certain sorts of social situations), as a corollary to one of Kelly\u2019s points try to make sure that a good portion of the time that happens there\u2019ll be witnesses if anyone flares their anima banner. Since Celestials will think at least twice about flaring while DBs all but specifically <i>want</i> to make a light show of things this will effectively reverse whose dice caps are higher in practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T18:21:33-07:00","id":1446205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446193#post1446193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, if there do end up being any DBs there needs to be VERY little overlap between their primary areas of expertise and those of the Celestials because anywhere there is overlap the DBs will be adding little in relative terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder how much games of Exalted ever involve the group splitting off into smaller sections so that they can attend to tasks in different areas. I remember when I talked about that one Lunar Manipulation Charm which lets the player retroactively declare that they were part of a scene the whole time, I got a number of people telling me that it is indeed relatively common to split up in such a manner, such that there would be dramatic value and functional utility in getting to a scene that logically should have presented a long distance and several obstacles.<br /> <br /> This is to suggest that a Dragon Blood joined in common purpose to some Celestial Exalted doesn't need to be joined to all of them by the hip, and that there are several axes by which they might be a valuable member of the split off portion.<br /> <br /> Mind, even in cases of similar areas of expertise, I feel as though there should be ways for a Dragon Blood to play to their strengths to be a valid actor in the scene in concert with the Solar or whomever. Picture the double act of the Dragon Blooded and Solar Investigators, whereby the Terrestrial does things like secure an invitation into the house of somebody to interrogate and binds it with Warrant of Divine Safety, ensuring that he and his Solar companion cannot be harmed or thrown out while they conduct their business. And even from the scene thereafter, they get to enhance effectiveness or efficiency by dealing with separate topics at the same time; the Solar focuses on questioning the residents while the Dragon Blood examines the area (or perhaps vice versa, depending on the social context or the particulars of what they're looking for). I'd have to compare Charm sets more closely, but I think the Terrestrial Charms have a few particular effects that Solar Charms don't exactly capture.<br /> <br /> Or even if they do, one can lean into the aspect of divided efforts allowing one to cover more ground and gain an even more precise picture of what went on. That and just... treating it as a double act means playing into the thing as though they're friends. Doing the stock buddy cop thing of treating who takes point on an interrogation as a matter of reciprocal courtesy rather than measuring whose process is more technically efficient. Sometimes you just feel like getting the truth out of somebody by lighting your hands on fire and working them over, you know?<br /> <br /> {Does a bit of comparison}<br /> <br /> Actually, one of those times might be when the scene turns violent and Irresistible Questioning Technique becomes free to resist. Shadow-Immolating Talon can only be resisted if answering would violate a Defining Intimacy, and even then the subject is required to say <i>something</i> that can be followed up on. Also, the Solar Charm in question can only be used once per session on the same character, whereas Shadow-Immolating Technique can be used once per scene. One could have a session in which the Solar questions in an early scene, gets enough answers for a lead but not enough to extract warning of danger they might walk into, and then in a scene after that danger the duo returns with a sense that the Terrestrial is going to need to play the Bad Cop to find out the rest of what the person knew.<br /> <br /> I don't know, stuff off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> Also, there's that whole thing of how the game system rewards players for deliberately ceding the spotlight of a scene to another player or supporting them in an expression of their character focus. You don't reap any payment for going out of your way to override another player's character or put their contributions down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 04-27-2021, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T19:12:52-07:00","id":1446212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1445737#post1445737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say be mindful of the dice cap. If an enemy (Ahlat, Octavian) can add what is essentially +10 dice on a roll then the Lunars and Solars can match that. The DB can only add 6. It is very difficult for the Dragonblooded to match this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it necessary to match those numbers for every possible contribution that a Dragon Blooded character might make to a fight against Ahlat, looking across the full range of their powers?<br /> <br /> Also, I can't recall, does Ahlat have Charms that allow him to attack more than one person at a time? Does he have negators for penalties on his Defence? I think either deficiency adds complications for one more person for him to choose to attack or be required to defend against. The latter in particular if a few extra notches to his Defence mean a few more points lost to a Solar's withering attack, so that next round his dice cap is less than ten.<br /> <br /> And Solars and Lunars do have some nice Defend Other Charms to help keep their less strong allies in the game.<br /> <br /> If Ahlat chooses to try expending his Initiative on the Dragon Blood for being the apparent weak link in the fight, Portentous Comet Deflection to clash the decisive attack might produce better results than pitting Defence against it. I mean, competing dice pools might have a better shot than letting his dice pool roll against a difficulty. How many dice is it against the Terrestrial's 16 dice, 25? A risky gamble, but perhaps not an insurmountable one, and the reward is getting to roll <b>your</b> Initiative (and whatever damage adders) against <i>his</i> Health, which might have been more difficult against his Defence. Maybe you add some wound penalties at an inopportune time. Maybe you move him close enough to death to reassess his priorities or put him on the back hoof.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, should the character survive the encounter, &quot;I pitted blade against blade with the Southern War God and scratched his hide&quot; is quite a story for a Terrestrial Exalt to tell in the caravansaries and spirit courts of those lands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T04:12:19-07:00","id":1446267,"title":"","content":"I mean I say &quot;if Ahlat chooses&quot;, but of course Ahlat isn't a person, he doesn't make decisions. The Storyteller makes decisions. The Storyteller decides whether or not the big nasty is going to direct his attack at one of the less powerful characters to give their player the chance to shine or make a significant contribution by the use of any number of defensive options. The Storyteller has numerous options for making this decision plausible to the character, ranging from &quot;judges them to be most vulnerable to advance the fight&quot; to &quot;has more beef with Dragon Blooded out of the last several centuries of dealing with them&quot;.<br /> <br /> I feel as though in conversations like this we don't talk enough about the interesting and impressive things characters can do in a responsive position and that the direction of incoming challenges is governed by a Storyteller who ought to have priorities for dramatic scenarios and distributed player engagement. Just as a contrary point and additional consideration to the idea that Dragon Blooded players necessarily end up with nothing to do when Celestial Exalted are also around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T07:33:19-07:00","id":1446286,"title":"","content":"Another way to make the DB feel more empowered is to have a game in a Realm-controlled region, you know, *properly* controlled, with military power, legions, and the rest. The DBs don't even have to be dynasts.<br /> <br /> Given the near-certainty of the celestials being in a very difficult situation if they give a hint of being anathema, they have to use their wonderful powers in a very controlled and discreet way. Conversely, the DBs will be openly respected and openly use every Charm and glow whenever they want. <br /> <br /> This can go sideways pretty fast, if the players don't have the maturity or willingness to keep their glow hidden for a whole campaign. You should not threaten the players with overwhelming force and having nothing happen if they glow to bonfire anima in front of Legion headquarters. But it is viable to have a campaign like this with the right players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T14:15:24-07:00","id":1446329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446212#post1446212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it necessary to match those numbers for every possible contribution that a Dragon Blooded character might make to a fight against Ahlat, looking across the full range of their powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any dice pool the Dragonblooded is going to make against Alhat, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446212#post1446212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I can't recall, does Ahlat have Charms that allow him to attack more than one person at a time? Does he have negators for penalties on his Defence? I think either deficiency adds complications for one more person for him to choose to attack or be required to defend against. The latter in particular if a few extra notches to his Defence mean a few more points lost to a Solar's withering attack, so that next round his dice cap is less than ten.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some things are factors, but that is the general ballpark. Also if you're 4 or more dice behind Ahlat? Then it's probably a reasonable bet that you also don't have a huge investment in combat charms and your only option would be holding out until the combat monkey arrives or find a more peaceful solution. If you are already in combat, then your time and effort would probably be better spent on things not directly related to offense against Alhat (I.E. attacking).<br /> <br /> Also we've had a thread talking about dicepool averages vs NPC defense, one that lasted 10+ pages. I'm not repeating myself in detail, but most players I've seen would contribute to a scene rather than be an over-glorified onslaught shaving bot that Bob the Rookie Guardsman can do just as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446212#post1446212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Solars and Lunars do have some nice Defend Other Charms to help keep their less strong allies in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>A good way to keep alive, but if you're expecting to do something directly offensive to Alhat? It's going to be much harder for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446212#post1446212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Ahlat chooses to try expending his Initiative on the Dragon Blood for being the apparent weak link in the fight, Portentous Comet Deflection to clash the decisive attack might produce better results than pitting Defence against it.<b> I mean, competing dice pools might have a better shot than letting his dice pool roll against a difficulty.</b> How many dice is it against the Terrestrial's 16 dice, 25? A risky gamble, but perhaps not an insurmountable one, and the reward is getting to roll <b>your</b> Initiative (and whatever damage adders) against <i>his</i> Health, which might have been more difficult against his Defence. Maybe you add some wound penalties at an inopportune time. Maybe you move him close enough to death to reassess his priorities or put him on the back hoof.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahlat has a base accuracy of 14 dice. If he adds things up to about 19 dice? Things are going to be tough but possible.<br /> <br /> If Ahlat has a full excellency of 24 dice? He has a 54% chance to roll 12 successes, hell getting 10 is 77%. The DB has a 55% chance of eight successes and a 27% chance of hitting 10. Forget about hitting 12. Not only did you consume your attack roll not hitting him, but he also hits you and beans you in the balls very hard, resulting in the penalties for losing a clash.<br /> <br /> Yes, this changes if the Dragonblooded has Crossfire Slash, to the point where an Essence 3 DB has near equal odds. This is regarded as having some method of combat investment, and is a consideration for the three dice thumbstick I give out. But if you're going just straight dice vs dice then at that point you're playing Exalted: Las Vegas edition. A player without significant combat investment is going to run into a brick wall or feel like they're not doing as much. At most they'll have to bide their time to wait until Ahlat has lower initiative for his excellency, find something else to do, or ask their teammates for assistance in order not to become pinata for Ahlat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446267#post1446267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean I say &quot;if Ahlat chooses&quot;, but of course Ahlat isn't a person, he doesn't make decisions. The Storyteller makes decisions. The Storyteller decides whether or not the big nasty is going to direct his attack at one of the less powerful characters to give their player the chance to shine or make a significant contribution by the use of any number of defensive options. The Storyteller has numerous options for making this decision plausible to the character, ranging from &quot;judges them to be most vulnerable to advance the fight&quot; to &quot;has more beef with Dragon Blooded out of the last several centuries of dealing with them&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the same thing as the rule zero fallacy. At most I can see Ahlat not attacking you if you don't take out a weapon (unless you run, then you're likely to get an arrow in the back due to his intimacies and if he has a free moment to shoot). But if you take out a weapon with intent to use it on Ahlat? Then you are a possible target.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446267#post1446267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though in conversations like this we don't talk enough about the interesting and impressive things characters can do in a responsive position and that the direction of incoming challenges is governed by a Storyteller who ought to have priorities for dramatic scenarios and distributed player engagement. Just as a contrary point and additional consideration to the idea that Dragon Blooded players necessarily end up with nothing to do when Celestial Exalted are also around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying Dragonblooded players can do nothing. I know that is false. I just think it is disingenuous to expect Dragonblooded to be able to keep up with the Celestial, or even the plantonic version of Solars, without some sort of concessions or bones thrown the Dragonblooded's way. Likewise if the Storyteller knows he's throwing an enemy at the group which a player is very mathematically disadvantaged against, goes against the players theme/goal for the character (I.E. be the big damn hero), and the Storyteller possesses the knowledge of said math and fails to notify the player about this or chooses to continue? Whatever happens next is the Storyteller's face.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T16:21:39-07:00","id":1446370,"title":"","content":"Don't elemental styles help against someone like Alhat? I'll admit it's been a while since the Aura keyword has completely turned me off using dragon blooded in any RAW way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T17:34:44-07:00","id":1446378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446329#post1446329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also we've had a thread talking about dicepool averages vs NPC defense, one that lasted 10+ pages. I'm not repeating myself in detail, but most players I've seen would contribute to a scene rather than be an over-glorified onslaught shaving bot that Bob the Rookie Guardsman can do just as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to argue again with Sandact about this, but for Citadel's sake, I believe this is not true.<br /> <br /> <br /> Alhat alone will get punked out like a little bitch going 5v1 against even marginally invested combat exalts. He's got a base parry of 6, so anyone with at least 12 dice on a withering attack can hit him quite reliably, which is to say 3 Dexterity, 3 melee, a specialty in daiklaves, a daiklave, and just 2m into the excellency. He's got things like Whirlwind Dervish Defense, and depending on your reading of Boundless War-God Arete, which can boost it, but those are initiative and motes limited, and good luck doing that 6+ times every round. Even if he had the initiative to do it he'd last less than 2 rounds before becoming completely mote-tapped.<br /> <br /> To elaborate, Whirlwind Dervish Defense costs initiative to use, so it can't be used if he doesn't have the initiative for it, and his excellency is only up to (current initiative, maximum 10) meaning when he's crashed he can not add dice at all with it, and after a decisive attack he can only add 3.<br /> <br /> So Alhat isn't much of a threat on his own, except to a very young and inexperienced circle who are not very focused on combat. Which makes some sense, he's the second most powerful war god in Exalted, after Mars. Because of that though, he needs backup to become any kind of effective. The kind of backup that he gets might be in the form of his brides, who have a pretty impressive Evasion 5, but only a soak of 4, and no ability to negate penalties of any kind.<br /> <br /> So if your character isn't as crazy combat focused as the Dawn, those allies to Alhat are the ones you should be focusing on. Alhat needs those helper characters to be effective, take them out and you're golden.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446329#post1446329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the same thing as the rule zero fallacy. At most I can see Ahlat not attacking you if you don't take out a weapon (unless you run, then you're likely to get an arrow in the back due to his intimacies and if he has a free moment to shoot). But if you take out a weapon with intent to use it on Ahlat? Then you are a possible target.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also this is not always the case. The Dawn who just crashed Alhat, and how has 30 initiative while saying &quot;ka...me...<i>ha</i>...<i>me</i>....&quot; is the one that Alhat should be attacking, because he's about to slay him on his next turn. I suppose it's possible in that circumstance that Alhat would direct a spiteful withering attack at somebody else, but it really doesn't make any sense for him to do so.<br /> <br /> <br /> And again, consider:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Dawn: Then I had him right where I wanted him, the Southern God of War lined up right in my bowsights, and he chooses instead to flail at old birch tree over here, haha, *cough cough*. Anyway, so I ended up taking his head clean off.<br /> <br /> Sycophant: Truly an epic tale my glorious Solar lord. If I may say, however, so boldly, my lord has been looking somewhat pale these past few days, and has hardly touched his feast this evening.<br /> <br /> Dawn: Nonsense, just haven't been getting much sleep late- *burbs up black spittle, frothing and running down his chin*<br /> <br /> Wood Aspect: I told you to let me examine you.<br /> <br /> Dawn: And <i>I</i> told <i>you</i> that I need no assistance from a mere terrestrial exa- *pushes hard away from the banquet table, stumbling to all fours as he pukes a stream of black bile*<br /> <br /> Wood Aspect: Nobody touch that black stuff, unless you're very interested to know what it feels like to vomit your lungs through your throat.<br /> <br /> Dawn: Hah, weak mortals. *spews another river of foulness*<br /> <br /> Wood Aspect: Not this time, it'll get you too. *wrapping a leaf around some kind of hard pellet from her pouch*<br /> <br /> Dawn: Nonsense, I'll be fine.<br /> <br /> Wood Aspect: You know, once your stomach goes it's really a tossup. You've lost a lot of fluid, you <i>might </i>die of dehydration first, which is slow, sickening, but at least it's less horrifying than feeling your more vital organs exit your body of their own volition. I would find watching you die very upsetting either way, but the dehydration would at least leave a nicer body to bury.<br /> <br /> Dawn: FINE! Give it here, give it here, although I'm not sure how I'll keep it down. *dry heaves on the stone floor*<br /> <br /> Wood Aspect: My deepest apologies my friend, but you couldn't keep it down if you tried. If I'd examined you earlier and caught it yesterday you could have.<br /> <br /> Dawn: So what good are you? *dry heaves harder*<br /> <br /> Wood Aspect: It's not going in your mouth. Don't worry, I won't tell anyone, just remember this next time I say I need to examine you.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> At which point the Sidereal, who isn't quite as good an investigator as a Solar investigator would be, but is still awesome and has unique abilities Solars don't, goes off to figure out how their Dawn friend contracted such an illness.<br /> <br /> <br /> In that instance what good was the Dawn? Absolutely no good, totally useless, worse even than barely contributing in combat. Essentially the only person who shines in that scene is the wood aspect doctor. So is it really awful that during the previous fight scene the Dawn was the one saving everyone else? Maybe at your table, but I don't think so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T17:40:09-07:00","id":1446381,"title":"","content":"Back during the DB KS I made a DB in a group of all solars. She worked just fine. I'm not saying its a perfectly balanced thing but a nice thing was due to the fact many Exy's could do successes. A lot of social work doesn't need the massive dice pool of solars, as a couple successes can usually meet what you need. <br /> <br /> Another thing is knowing your role. She was a performer in the Eclipse' circus. She was pretending to be a mortal who was ACTING as a fire aspect. (hiding from her traitorous uncle). As a fire aspect she was skilled in swordplay but wasn't better in a fight than the combat invested solars. But she wasn't in anyway useless, especially as she was the only one who used mounted combat with a fire horse. (modified Aughdeihe). As the Jade Phoenix Soul her whole thing was being a distracting presence in her performances. This allowed others ability to do things while eyes were on her. <br /> <br /> Now would I have changed some things? yeah, now that the book has fully been out for a while some things would have changed. I would have also requested some of the balancing stuff from above like a free signature, or changing the XP to various essence ratings. But if you talk with the other players on what to expect, make sure to find roles, and have the ST give everyone time to shine, the game can work. Its tricky but it can happen.<br /> <br /> Lunars and Solars on the other hand work just fine together. I've yet to run into a problem where Specialized McSupernal and Adaptable McBroadskill can't work well together. It's important to remember that Solars have a supernal, which gives them a lot of power in one field, and their starter charms in anything they invest in usually bring a strong power to bear. Lunars can become the bear. Their toolkit is absurdly applicable, and due to how they can just add to it by doing a murder, they are VERY capable of having a way to solve problems. <br /> <br /> The key things are it depends on the table, the ST, and what you are looking to get out of the game. I've done mixed very well and thrived as the lone DB among celestials, but i'm probably the exception and not the rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T11:16:07-07:00","id":1446464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446370#post1446370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't elemental styles help against someone like Alhat? I'll admit it's been a while since the Aura keyword has completely turned me off using dragon blooded in any RAW way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Each dragon style has one or two specifically anti-spirit Charms, plus the general no-Terrestrial-keyword benefit, <i>and</i> they\u2019re all strictly mono-element so you only really need to worry about the aura rules if you\u2019re trying to mix two of them or use Dodge or Resistance Charms.<br /> <br /> Also I\u2019m really not sure how y\u2019all are forgetting Thousand Strikes Dance when it outright says in its own text that Ahlat uses it when outnumbered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 04-29-2021, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T11:59:42-07:00","id":1446471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446464#post1446464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Each dragon style has one or two specifically anti-spirit Charms, plus the general no-Terrestrial-keyword benefit, <i>and</i> they\u2019re all strictly mono-element so you only really need to worry about the aura rules if you\u2019re trying to mix two of them or use Dodge or Resistance Charms.<br /> <br /> Also I\u2019m really not sure how y\u2019all are forgetting Thousand Strikes Dance when it outright says in its own text that Ahlat uses it when outnumbered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah so Thousand Strikes as well as Ready in Eight Directions and the Abyssal version, are really...strange charms in Exalted.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a generally open system, you know when your opponent uses that charm, so you can opt to just not attack them. Alhat uses it, spends 15m and 1wp, and in response the whole circle just...aims. And then it comes around to his turn again, he regenerates 5m, but then spends another 15 and a willpower and again all the Solars just aim, and regen another 25m collectively...<br /> <br /> Unless there\u2019s something compelling you to attack Alhat, which he can\u2019t even do with social influence because he can\u2019t flurry simple charms, you just kind of sit there watching him drain all his motes and willpower, and then pounce on him with your +3 non-charm aim dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T12:33:39-07:00","id":1446644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446464#post1446464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Each dragon style has one or two specifically anti-spirit Charms, plus the general no-Terrestrial-keyword benefit, <i>and</i> they\u2019re all strictly mono-element so you only really need to worry about the aura rules if you\u2019re trying to mix two of them or use Dodge or Resistance Charms.<br /> <br /> Also I\u2019m really not sure how y\u2019all are forgetting Thousand Strikes Dance when it outright says in its own text that Ahlat uses it when outnumbered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just mean in general the aura keyword made a really decent charmset into a broken version of itself where dragon blooded are forced to take unusable charms to get usable ones and without a massive amount of homebrew most charms are locked out due to aura. <br /> <br /> I haven't played 3e much but for the sake of the dragon blooded character, i'd just make every dragon blooded omni arua.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T13:28:17-07:00","id":1446650,"title":"","content":"Eh, personally the only thing I\u2019d change is that trying to enter an aura of an element other than your aspect\u2019s while at bonfire results in aspect aura instead of no aura. You\u2019re right about the holes that badly need plugging where an Ability has a great Aura-keyworded Charm but no Charms for entering the right aura with but greatly exaggerating how many of them there are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T16:14:51-07:00","id":1446680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446650#post1446650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, personally the only thing I\u2019d change is that trying to enter an aura of an element other than your aspect\u2019s while at bonfire results in aspect aura instead of no aura. You\u2019re right about the holes that badly need plugging where an Ability has a great Aura-keyworded Charm but no Charms for entering the right aura with but greatly exaggerating how many of them there are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not. There literally needs to be 5 elemental trees for every element to make that charmset work. We don't even have a full elemental tree half the time they share with another element if not two. Melee is water and fire with water having the last two charms. You still need to get some of each to get the last ones. Meaning literal dead charms for which ever element you're going for. Then you have stuff like the sig grass dodge charm which doesn't work with almost any other charm except the two balance ones. Or the water athletics charm which is practically alone. The charmset without the keyword is great. With it, it's a mess for players. They have to specifically match the element, then they have to get the charms or they'll be locked out. Most times they'll still have to buy the early ones though. An omni-aura makes a dragon blooded slightly more powerful but it at least lets them use every charm they buy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-30-2021, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T01:23:06-07:00","id":1446757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446644#post1446644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't played 3e much but for the sake of the dragon blooded character, i'd just make every dragon blooded omni arua.</div> </div> </div> </div>Theory crafting? I absolutely agree with you.<br /> <br /> Actual play?<br /> <br /> RAW works.<br /> <br /> We've got an archer who mostly stays in Wood Aura, but has set up Air Aura to use their &quot;speedbump&quot; charms. It takes a bit of planning, but it works. (An Air Aspect archer might do better here, mostly staying in Wood Aura but sliding into Air with their anima power or going bonfire.)<br /> <br /> We've got a Fire Aspect Melee user who has something like 12 fire aspect charms, plus Evocations, plus Dodge charms who just sits in Fire Aura. She doesn't have any charms that are Wood/Water/Air/Earth Aspect. Like, sure, Mela\u2019s Flashing Tongue <i>exists</i>, but if you've got Burning Pinnacle Strike and Harnessed Firestorm Assault... you're not exactly disadvantaged not taking it.<br /> <br /> We've got a noncombat Air Aspect who just takes the five seconds it takes to enter the right Aura to do her thing outside of combat.<br /> <br /> And we got the Earth Aspect Immaculate who gets in Earth Aura and Bonfire Anima in turn one, then just wrecking-balls the rest of the combat with Earth Dragon Charms.<br /> <br /> And yes, that is limiting. A Water Aspect Swordfighter pretty much has to be a Single Point Stylist because Water Melee is all but unusable. Good luck being an Archer if you're a Fire Aspect. But if you're going out of your way to do something whacky in combat, then be prepared to homebrew -- you can't expect a cookie cutter solution to work if you intentionally break the mold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-01-2021, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T02:19:36-07:00","id":1446761,"title":"","content":"Because of the mentioned aura problem. In my experience during a pure DB game. Be <i>very</i> generous with homebrewing new charms. Maybe let players stunt to use a different element for charms. Soaring leap might be an explosion for fire or lashing with a vine for wood. One of my players uses an artifact made of green jade, all of the evocations are wood aspect because of it. <br /> <br /> I'm surprised this is not default and that not more charms were dual aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13615-slovorg","name":"slovorg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T06:43:35-07:00","id":1446787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446757#post1446757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theory crafting? I absolutely agree with you.<br /> <br /> Actual play?<br /> <br /> RAW works.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>The examples sound very limiting. Which was my problem with them. Dragon blooded already have a limited charmset, this just kneecaps players who want to do different combinations of skills and abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T09:32:00-07:00","id":1446803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446787#post1446787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The examples sound very limiting. Which was my problem with them. Dragon blooded already have a limited charmset, this just kneecaps players who want to do different combinations of skills and abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the idea was to preserve the matter of Dragon Blooded being the least powerful Exalted while giving them some more impressive effects by giving them an avenue they need to navigate through that keeps them from getting all the impressive stuff at the same time (in a manner that displays the elemental motif).<br /> <br /> It might not be for everybody, but not all combinations being functional is working as intended to preserve setting conceits but also include cool shit to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T11:48:28-07:00","id":1446818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446803#post1446803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, the idea was to preserve the matter of Dragon Blooded being the least powerful Exalted while giving them some more impressive effects by giving them an avenue they need to navigate through that keeps them from getting all the impressive stuff at the same time (in a manner that displays the elemental motif).<br /> <br /> It might not be for everybody, but not all combinations being functional is working as intended to preserve setting conceits but also include cool shit to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen people house rule that dbs are omni aura and only one charm that consumes aura can be used in a turn. They have a little more power while still being definitively weaker then celestials. I haven't heard of any balance issues yet and it lets someone take different abilities without needing to make a massive amount of homebrew. The issue with the keyword is that it requires a theoretical charmset that's 5x bigger than it is. Which is insane. It's easier to invalidate the keyword, and if any serious balance problems arise, fix those specific charms. Then it would be to make 5 seperate elemental charmsets for all 25 abilities. Especially when it's one db with celestials in the party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T12:21:14-07:00","id":1446824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446818#post1446818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've seen people house rule that dbs are omni aura and only one charm that consumes aura can be used in a turn. They have a little more power while still being definitively weaker then celestials. I haven't heard of any balance issues yet and it lets someone take different abilities without needing to make a massive amount of homebrew. The issue with the keyword is that it requires a theoretical charmset that's 5x bigger than it is. Which is insane. It's easier to invalidate the keyword, and if any serious balance problems arise, fix those specific charms. Then it would be to make 5 seperate elemental charmsets for all 25 abilities. Especially when it's one db with celestials in the party.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue with the omni-aura thing is that it doesn't reward anyone for focusing on one single element, so your best option is always just to be the Avatar, master of all elements. Which isn't necessarily bad, but it was a design goal that choosing to focus on just one element would be viable. You give up Demon-Crushing Wolf Bite and Graceful Flowing Defense, but gain bonus power from Flame Warden Stance and Blazing Interception. Your best option isn't strictly to mix a ton of elements together, but it is an option.<br /> <br /> The reason the trees are out of order too is because charm cascades must follow a logical progression in style and power, so Mirror-on-Water Focus just can't branch off of Graceful Flowing Defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T14:30:09-07:00","id":1446849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446824#post1446824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The issue with the omni-aura thing is that it doesn't reward anyone for focusing on one single element, so your best option is always just to be the Avatar, master of all elements. Which isn't necessarily bad, but it was a design goal that choosing to focus on just one element would be viable. You give up Demon-Crushing Wolf Bite and Graceful Flowing Defense, but gain bonus power from Flame Warden Stance and Blazing Interception. Your best option isn't strictly to mix a ton of elements together, but it is an option.<br /> <br /> The reason the trees are out of order too is because charm cascades must follow a logical progression in style and power, so Mirror-on-Water Focus just can't branch off of Graceful Flowing Defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no tree that rewards you for focusing on any single element. Most of them punish you because half of the powerful charms are a separate element . Moreover the amount of charms you'd have to make to make an individual element viable is staggering. This isn't an issue of being the avatar or not. It's about making a viable character and how much homebrew you'd have to make to make it work. As Johndoe pointed out previously, Water melee isn't viable despite having a good chunk of the melee charmset. It's missing a number of core charms that let you take advantage of the later charms. That kind of design is just clunky and it doesn't particularly help a dragon blooded in a pure DB game let alone one where they are in a group with celestials who are capable of doing things x10 better. Even with an omni-aura, dragon blooded still distinctly under celestials. This is more for the sake of the dragon blooded having an easier time with their own build and concept. not having to take useless charms to get good ones.<br /> <br /> It'd be nice to have a charmset where every element is distinct but that would again, require many more charms then what we have. It's much easier to refluff them if you feel like they have to follow one element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T15:21:33-07:00","id":1446852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446849#post1446849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no tree that rewards you for focusing on any single element.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Aura keyword does, surely? If you decided to forego Graceful Flowing Defense and Demon-Crushing Wolf Bite to focus on only fire charms, you get to use the fire aura charms, and get the aura effects of other fire charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446849#post1446849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moreover the amount of charms you'd have to make to make an individual element viable is staggering. This isn't an issue of being the avatar or not. It's about making a viable character and how much homebrew you'd have to make to make it work. As Johndoe pointed out previously, Water melee isn't viable despite having a good chunk of the melee charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that water melee in particular is not viable, although some element-ability combinations are somewhat. You can grab.<br /> <br /> <br /> Balanced:<br /> Stoking Bonfire Style<br /> Flame-Borne Interception<br /> Burning Fury Wreath<br /> Wrath-Grounding Guard<br /> Blinding Spark Distraction<br /> Crossfire Flash<br /> Root-and-Hand Merging<br /> <br /> Water:<br /> Dragon Graced Weapon<br /> Elemental Sheath<br /> Graceful Flowing Defense<br /> Dragon Scale Shield<br /> Roaring River Slash<br /> Fire Incites Water to a Riot of Clouds<br /> Mirror-on-Water Focus<br /> <br /> Fire:<br /> Portentous Comet Deflection<br /> <br /> <br /> That's not exactly a tiny amount of charms, and the only one you have to get that doesn't mesh with your Water aura is Portentous Comet Deflection. It would be nice if you didn't have to get Portentous Comet Deflection, but Cloud Riot is a pretty big complex charm that wouldn't necessarily fit right coming off of just Crossfire Flash. There are also just some things that I think are mistakes, like they don't fit necessarily, but I think they just are mistakes, and they're few enough that I don't attribute any of them to lack of competence.<br /> <br /> <br /> There <i>are</i> some that aren't very viable, I don't think that Air Brawl is really that good, but I don't really see an easy solution to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T16:53:10-07:00","id":1446865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446852#post1446852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Aura keyword does, surely? If you decided to forego Graceful Flowing Defense and Demon-Crushing Wolf Bite to focus on only fire charms, you get to use the fire aura charms, and get the aura effects of other fire charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't think that water melee in particular is not viable, although some element-ability combinations are somewhat. You can grab.<br /> <br /> <br /> Balanced:<br /> Stoking Bonfire Style<br /> Flame-Borne Interception<br /> Burning Fury Wreath<br /> Wrath-Grounding Guard<br /> Blinding Spark Distraction<br /> Crossfire Flash<br /> Root-and-Hand Merging<br /> <br /> Water:<br /> Dragon Graced Weapon<br /> Elemental Sheath<br /> Graceful Flowing Defense<br /> Dragon Scale Shield<br /> Roaring River Slash<br /> Fire Incites Water to a Riot of Clouds<br /> Mirror-on-Water Focus<br /> <br /> Fire:<br /> Portentous Comet Deflection<br /> <br /> <br /> That's not exactly a tiny amount of charms, and the only one you have to get that doesn't mesh with your Water aura is Portentous Comet Deflection. It would be nice if you didn't have to get Portentous Comet Deflection, but Cloud Riot is a pretty big complex charm that wouldn't necessarily fit right coming off of just Crossfire Flash. There are also just some things that I think are mistakes, like they don't fit necessarily, but I think they just are mistakes, and they're few enough that I don't attribute any of them to lack of competence.<br /> <br /> <br /> There <i>are</i> some that aren't very viable, I don't think that Air Brawl is really that good, but I don't really see an easy solution to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do lose a bunch of charms though that are insanely useful. It's not as bad as other trees are though but still not great. A lot of the charms which are necessary and then you have charms which aren't but make a huge difference. Dragon Soul Burst and Burning pinnacle strike are two charms which an make a difference yet are locked out for a water master. Then there's the random ass Air melee charm at the end that requires 4 fire non-balanced charms to purchase. This feels like they made the charmset as a whole then broke it up with an unnecessary keyword, that honestly feels haphazardly tossed. Sometimes things that are B&amp;B don't have the balanced keywords sometimes very niche things do. It only causes me to reiterate the fact that you'd be better off refluffing out of aspect charms, then you would recreating the charmset 5 times for each element and finishing up the half created trees in the core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T17:09:44-07:00","id":1446867,"title":"","content":"The answer to \u201cHow do I [Ability] as [Aspect]\u201d is \u201cHave something with an anima cost to stay out of bonfire with.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T18:03:40-07:00","id":1446876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446867#post1446867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The answer to \u201cHow do I [Ability] as [Aspect]\u201d is \u201cHave something with an anima cost to stay out of bonfire with.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the only issue I'm talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T18:33:16-07:00","id":1446882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446865#post1446865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do lose a bunch of charms though that are insanely useful. It's not as bad as other trees are though but still not great. A lot of the charms which are necessary and then you have charms which aren't but make a huge difference. Dragon Soul Burst and Burning pinnacle strike are two charms which an make a difference yet are locked out for a water master. Then there's the random ass Air melee charm at the end that requires 4 fire non-balanced charms to purchase. This feels like they made the charmset as a whole then broke it up with an unnecessary keyword, that honestly feels haphazardly tossed. Sometimes things that are B&amp;B don't have the balanced keywords sometimes very niche things do. It only causes me to reiterate the fact that you'd be better off refluffing out of aspect charms, then you would recreating the charmset 5 times for each element and finishing up the half created trees in the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the way Mela's Flashing Tongue is supposed to work is that you start the fight and battle in Fire aura, and then when you hit bonfire and auto-switch to Air aura your next turn you use MFT as a big finisher move. Maybe that's too niche of a use, but it does work. Also yes the water master is locked out of Burning Pinnacle Strike, but the fire master who uses Burning Pinnacle Strike is locked out of the defense penalty negator, which can be pretty dangerous when fighting against multiple opponents or in a situation where you're receiving lots of environmental/poison/wound penalties. I think overall fire is better, but water isn't useless garbage.<br /> <br /> Which is about the same for every ability, at least that I can think of off the top of my head. If you're going single element brawl then water is the most powerful one to do that, single element archery wood is the most powerful option. Which isn't to say that going mixed aspect or out of aspect is bad. I mean, we're in a thread about playing a DB in a mixed game, if you're playing a DB when you could play a Solar you're already choosing to not be as powerful as you could be. Some of the out of aspect things are pretty cool though and worth doing anyway.<br /> <br /> It could have been done better I think, but as it is it's not broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T00:59:33-07:00","id":1446924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446849#post1446849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no tree that rewards you for focusing on any single element. [...] As Johndoe pointed out previously, Water melee isn't viable despite having a good chunk of the melee charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Melee rewards you INSANELY for focusing on Fire.<br /> <br /> All the charm trees reward you for going hard &quot;in aspect&quot;. That's literally what the aura mechanic does.<br /> <br /> Water Melee, as DrLoveMonkey points out, is &quot;fine&quot;. But if your character concept is defined as a swordfighter, then you're in for a bad time -- you will not remotely keep pace with a Fire Swordfighter using native DB melee charms. If you're playing a Gentleman Thief or a Naval Strategist, then Water Melee is more than sufficient to round out a little combat capability on the side.<br /> <br /> That's because Melee is a Fire Ability. If you want a unique and quirky character, that's not going to work fresh out the box. You're going to have to create custom charms to support your concept. That's a feature, not a bug.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1446849#post1446849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's missing a number of core charms that let you take advantage of the later charms. That kind of design is just clunky and it doesn't particularly help a dragon blooded in a pure DB game let alone one where they are in a group with celestials who are capable of doing things x10 better. Even with an omni-aura, dragon blooded still distinctly under celestials. This is more for the sake of the dragon blooded having an easier time with their own build and concept. not having to take useless charms to get good ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, this is a problem if you're theorycrafting.<br /> <br /> &quot;What if I want to play an Archer? But I don't want to be a celestial, and I don't want to be a Wood or Air Aspect... I wonder if I can make an Earth Aspect Archer who can go kill Octavian? Wait... no I can't?!? THE GAME IS BROKEN!&quot;<br /> <br /> Thing is... in a real game, if you wanted to play an archer... you probably would pick Wood or Air Aspect to support your concept. Just like you wouldn't make an Eclipse Archer and claim that Dawn Archers make your concept unviable because all the good Charms are locked behind Essence requirements and only Dawns get Supernal Archery. And even if you did make an Earth Aspect Archer, your ST would tailor encounters to fit the party -- they won't TPK you on Session 1 with a party of Five Octavians because you dared to bring an Earth Archer to the table. <br /> <br /> Exalted isn't a DPS Challenge.<br /> <br /> In a real game, you will have &quot;good&quot; charms on your sheet that you don't use (because you don't remember them, or you're out of motes, or whatever). And a good ST will note your XP expenditure and shoehorn in a challenge now and then so you can use your speedbump &quot;useless&quot; charms. <br /> <br /> No-one likes a chore. And if building DBs with the aura mechanic is not fun for you, then use that Golden Rule and fix it. I really, really, don't like &quot;Duration: Aura&quot; -- it's a real fun slayer in my opinion and I like to houserule it to &quot;Keyword: Aura; Duration: Scene&quot;. <br /> <br /> But barring a couple of Charms that want Aura but provide no means of getting in Aura (can't remember what they are offhand), the Charmset isn't &quot;broken&quot;, it just wants a bit if polish here and there. It might not be to your taste, but I like it.<br /> <br /> I like Aura as a peaking mechanic that let's Deebs spike high and punch above their weight. Omni-aura would very much dilute what I want from Dragon-Blooded. It's not a bad idea, but I don't think it intrinsically would help with running a Terrestial in a Celestial game. And I don't agree that giving a straight buff to a splat makes it easier to build the character you want. Having a Session 0 to discuss the expectations of the game and building characters as a party makes it easier to build the character you want. Not hitting some arbitrary DPS threshold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T10:21:32-07:00","id":1446997,"title":"","content":"The problem is that this is an issue across the board. What does a wood stylist get to defend themselves? Dodge is bad, so is Resistance. What about a character who's focused on larceny but isn't Air? Why is that I have to literally make a concept based around an aspect instead of a concept based around a person? The aura mechanic just forces a situation where you can't do anything more than a hand full of options without massive amounts of homebrew. I honestly haven't seen Aura let DBs spike higher then their weight. In fact, it seems underwhelming to use a lot of charms out of aura. I'm not talking about an arbitrary DPS threshold. I'm talking about having fun with a character. It's not fun having to take speedbump charms. It's not fun being locked out of charms. Especially not during combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 05-02-2021, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T20:15:08-07:00","id":1447093,"title":"","content":"...Did someone tell you that (e.g.-) Wood Aspects can only use Wood Charms? Is that what\u2019s going on here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T20:47:00-07:00","id":1447095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1447093#post1447093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Did someone tell you that (e.g.-) Wood Aspects can only use Wood Charms? Is that what\u2019s going on here?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Aura keyword is insanely important it makes a lot of barely functional charms useful. It's required for a lot of the better charms, and the entire charmset is based around getting into aura pretty quickly or else you're going to be mediocre until you do. I don't think you realize the extent of aura and what it means for the characters. And yes you don't automatically hit bonfire but when start using charms you'll rapidly have that issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 05-03-2021, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T21:05:03-07:00","id":1447098,"title":"","content":"Wood aspects actually have good defense options in Dodge, at least close to what fire has. The only fire charms that help you defend are Flickering Candle Meditation, Bonfire Shadow Evasion, and Coiling Dragon Dance, and that last one is Essence 4. Meanwhile Wood has Swaying Grass Elusion, a cap bursting evasion booster that lets you reach Solar levels of defense boosting.<br /> <br /> Is fire better at dodging? Yeah probably a bit, but Wood can dodge just fine, the wood anima is even a dodge penalty negator. Or if you wanted to you could just forget about getting wood aura and use the fire dodge charms anyway, or even just be careful about your bonfire anima and use the fire aura of the charms if you want to.<br /> <br /> Resistance is pretty similar, Impervious Skin of Stone is balanced, and the only other direct soak boosting charm is water based. Meanwhile Wood, although less omni-applicable, lets your dodge based character wear medium armour, which is a flat +3 soak/hardness booster if you're not relying on parry. As for protection against decisive damage, water has a charm at Essence 1, Earth has the signature, but wood has a signature that heals decisive damage, Earth Bears Witness can be a wood, earth or water charm, and water has another two past that.<br /> <br /> I will say that I think it was a mistake to put an air aura charm after two water aura charms in Resistance, and Revolving Hurricane Force should have just come off something else somewhere.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T21:14:57-07:00","id":1447100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1447095#post1447095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Aura keyword is insanely important it makes a lot of barely functional charms useful. It's required for a lot of the better charms, and the entire charmset is based around getting into aura pretty quickly or else you're going to be mediocre until you do. I don't think you realize the extent of aura and what it means for the characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't care about aura though it lets you combo a lot of other charms together, or pick and choose however you want. A DB brawler who doesn't get into aura combines Oaken Thew Exertion, with Hammering Wave Technique, and Flotsam-and-Jetsam Approach to get +10 damage and use her strength to calculate accuracy on the attack. Or combines Pounding Surf Style with Stone Fist Strike to make an unarmed smash attack with a variable but potentially large amount of bonus overwhelming, and neither of those combos have to wait for turn 2 to get aura up, like any combo that relies on aura otherwise does.<br /> <br /> Plus then on the defense you can activate Eternal Tide Endurance with the Wood Protection Technique, and trigger Unfeeling Earth Meditation to boost your defense all at the same time. Again, you can do this even before your first turn in the combat because you don't require the aura.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T22:32:52-07:00","id":1447114,"title":"","content":"^ THIS. The Aura keyword means \u201cRequires one turn of setup.\u201d No more, no less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T03:07:18-07:00","id":1447157,"title":"","content":"It also means you you can't combine non elemental charms charms or you lose aura and when you hit bonfire, you no longer have access to those charms. It also doesn't help, like I said before that a number of charms are just worthless without aura.<br /> <br /> Like I said before the only reason to get rid of it is because you don't want to homebrew a bunch of charms. If the charmset was bigger it could work as is the st would be better off house ruling it so the dragon blooded doesn't get hamstringed. Nothing is really convincing me that dragon blooded are broken with it and previous editions didn't have this issue. They certainly had other issues but I can't use charms because I'm in my anima was not one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 05-03-2021, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T08:23:57-07:00","id":1447201,"title":"","content":"Not using certain Charms together is part of \u201cone turn of setup,\u201d you can still use whatever you want the rest of the time.<br /> <br /> The only time you <i>need</i> a custom Charm is when, for example, you want to use Roaring River Slash or Mirror-on-Water Focus as a non-Water Aspect but literally can\u2019t enter Water Aura because all the other Water Melee Charms are defensive. A ridiculous problem, sure, but one that takes exactly one new Charm to fix each time you run into it and is almost exclusively a Signature Charm problem in the first place.<br /> <br /> You keep acting like you have to permanently commit to one element per Ability and that\u2019s just not the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T09:44:17-07:00","id":1447218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1447201#post1447201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not using certain Charms together is part of \u201cone turn of setup,\u201d you can still use whatever you want the rest of the time.<br /> <br /> The only time you <i>need</i> a custom Charm is when, for example, you want to use Roaring River Slash or Mirror-on-Water Focus as a non-Water Aspect but literally can\u2019t enter Water Aura because all the other Water Melee Charms are defensive. A ridiculous problem, sure, but one that takes exactly one new Charm to fix each time you run into it and is almost exclusively a Signature Charm problem in the first place.<br /> <br /> You keep acting like you have to permanently commit to one element per Ability and that\u2019s just not the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to commit to your own unless you're very good at not using enough motes to hit anima. Which is much easier out of combat then it is in combat but still an issue. The bigger issue is that it's not just one or two charms for certain elements, it's entire trees. I just feel that the amount of charms presented is too little for every combination of dragon blooded. It requires a massive amount of homebrew and you'd be better off utilizing a short cut rather than keeping something that was too ambitous for it's own good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T14:47:33-07:00","id":1447273,"title":"","content":"Again, anima costs. And again, it takes exactly ONE Charm to fix \u201c[Ability] has uses for [Element] Aura but no way to enter it.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T15:57:26-07:00","id":1447286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1447273#post1447273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, anima costs. And again, it takes exactly ONE Charm to fix \u201c[Ability] has uses for [Element] Aura but no way to enter it.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more than that. It takes one charm to exit it too. I feel I've defended my point. If you feel it's fine. That's nice. I don't agree. I was giving my advice after making a water dragon stylist who had shit for defensive charms because all the good ones were out of element. The game didn't happen while I was creating the character but it would have required a lot of homebrew. Even from looking at my old character, aura isn't a fun mechanic at all. It's unnecessarily restrictive, and it's only fixed by a person doing it themselves. The charmsets are in theory infinite. The issue is when you have to make a new set of elemental charms a character.<br /> <br /> I'm done. I feel I've put out my point and we are just arguing in circles. While it is more limited then other people, I'd still suggest that citadel's DB character consider being omni aura to make the experience a lot more freer in concept. Even with omniaura I've never heard of a situation where the characters were busted but if it does happen, you can again tone down specific charms rather than having to homebrew a bunch of new ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 05-03-2021, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T20:54:33-07:00","id":1447521,"title":"","content":"<i>...I\u2019m so confused now.</i> Which Resistance Signature or Revolving Hurricane-Force Defense were you so badly hoping to use with Water Dragon Style that not being able to ruined Dragon-Blooded for you? You\u2019re not even giving up the pseudo-Mastery effects here, all the other soak/hardness/damage-reduction Charms are either Balanced, Water, or have a Water mini-purchase so you should absolutely still be starting all your turns in Water Aura.<br /> <br /> Or were you planning to get your Dodge on alongside a martial art that\u2019s compatible with medium armor?<br /> <br /> You keep describing problems that literally do not exist. This isn\u2019t a difference of opinion, you\u2019re just wrong about what\u2019s in Charmset and how Elemental Aura works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T21:48:14-07:00","id":1447524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1447521#post1447521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>...I\u2019m so confused now.</i> Which Resistance Signature or Revolving Hurricane-Force Defense were you so badly hoping to use with Water Dragon Style that not being able to ruined Dragon-Blooded for you? You\u2019re not even giving up the pseudo-Mastery effects here, all the other soak/hardness/damage-reduction Charms are either Balanced, Water, or have a Water mini-purchase so you should absolutely still be starting all your turns in Water Aura.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay now I'm also confused, Water Dragon is a very defensive style. It has a damage based PD, and a charm that lets you get a +2 non-charm defense bonus, and a defensive form charm. Taking resistance charms past that is going to be more a waste of motes than anything. If you have Stamina 4, and medium artifact armor you have a base soak of 12, which becomes 16 in the form, then 20 with Impervious Skin of Stone, +1 for every 1 on your enemy's attack roll with Eternal Tide Endurance. That's enough to soak Alhat's Bloodspike Spear down to minimum damage even if he overflows your defense by 5 on the attack.<br /> <br /> Or if you're looking to boost defense just go Flowing Water Defense with an attack to gain +2 non-charm evasion, which you can combo with your excellency to get Solar tier defense.<br /> <br /> If you were desperate for more defense than that you could always just get another MA instead of Dodge anyway, like White Reaper or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 05-05-2021, 12:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T05:33:05-07:00","id":1447563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1447521#post1447521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>...I\u2019m so confused now.</i> Which Resistance Signature or Revolving Hurricane-Force Defense were you so badly hoping to use with Water Dragon Style that not being able to ruined Dragon-Blooded for you? You\u2019re not even giving up the pseudo-Mastery effects here, all the other soak/hardness/damage-reduction Charms are either Balanced, Water, or have a Water mini-purchase so you should absolutely still be starting all your turns in Water Aura.<br /> <br /> Or were you planning to get your Dodge on alongside a martial art that\u2019s compatible with medium armor?<br /> <br /> You keep describing problems that literally do not exist. This isn\u2019t a difference of opinion, you\u2019re just wrong about what\u2019s in Charmset and how Elemental Aura works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was planning on taking dodge yes because in most cases the monk would still be in no or light armor. Resistance is fine but the character felt like a dodge character and multiple MA styles felt inapropriate. I was also going to round out the build with some athletics and that just wasn't going to happen. I know how the elemental aura works. It's clunky and certain charms are worthless with out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T06:07:40-07:00","id":1447569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1447563#post1447563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was planning on taking dodge yes because in most cases the monk would still be in no or light armor. Resistance is fine but the character felt like a dodge character and multiple MA styles felt inapropriate. I was also going to round out the build with some athletics and that just wasn't going to happen. I know how the elemental aura works. It's clunky and certain charms are worthless with out.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would the later Dodge charms even get you that you aren\u2019t getting from MA though? You could use Dodge and activate Flickering Candle Meditation, which is an unreliable charm that ignores penalties based on opponents\u2019s 1s, or use MA and get an automatic +2 non charm parry. Until Essence 3 that\u2019s the only non-excellency dodge charm that actually gives you a defense boost. If your issue is that you aren\u2019t wearing armour so you need the best defense value possible, Water Dragon in Water Aura is actually better than Dodge in Fire Aura anyway. Even at Essence 3, true Fire gets Bonfire Shadow Evasion, but you get Flow With Strife, which is a mini-Heavenly Guardian Defense. <br /> <br /> Your best supplement would definitely not be to go dodge, since you\u2019re already capbursting your defense with WD, but to go resistance to shore up your lack of soak from armour. If you wanted dodge no matter what that\u2019s","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T06:40:24-07:00","id":1447572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1447569#post1447569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What would the later Dodge charms even get you that you aren\u2019t getting from MA though? You could use Dodge and activate Flickering Candle Meditation, which is an unreliable charm that ignores penalties based on opponents\u2019s 1s, or use MA and get an automatic +2 non charm parry. Until Essence 3 that\u2019s the only non-excellency dodge charm that actually gives you a defense boost. If your issue is that you aren\u2019t wearing armour so you need the best defense value possible, Water Dragon in Water Aura is actually better than Dodge in Fire Aura anyway. Even at Essence 3, true Fire gets Bonfire Shadow Evasion, but you get Flow With Strife, which is a mini-Heavenly Guardian Defense. <br /> <br /> Your best supplement would definitely not be to go dodge, since you\u2019re already capbursting your defense with WD, but to go resistance to shore up your lack of soak from armour. If you wanted dodge no matter what that\u2019s</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a character and a concept and it wasn't really working within the system and yes. I know resistance has more useful applications and dodge is a little weak. I was fine with that except for the fact that half the charms didn't work in water aura. The way athletics worked and the lack of useful water athletics charms was another issue because it plays such a heavy role in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T15:51:44-07:00","id":1447649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1445666-running-a-lunar-solar-and-db-campaign-any-issues?p=1447572#post1447572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had a character and a concept and it wasn't really working within the system and yes. I know resistance has more useful applications and dodge is a little weak. I was fine with that except for the fact that half the charms didn't work in water aura. The way athletics worked and the lack of useful water athletics charms was another issue because it plays such a heavy role in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going really hard athletics rushing is a bit harder to do going mono-water. Crashing Tide Advance and Soaring Leap Technique are usable, but Bellows Pumping Stride isn't.<br /> <br /> If you're doing it that often though you might just think about breaking Aura. Combo the excellency with Bellows Pumping Stride, Soaring Leap Technique, Dancing Ember Stride, Verdant Dragon's Footsteps, and Flying Dagger Leap to get a rush that...<ul><li>Adds 1 non-charm die for every 10 on the roll</li> <li>Adds 1 non-charm die for every 1 on your opponent's roll</li> <li>Ignore plant based difficult terrain penalties and fatigue penalties</li> <li>Every 10 rerolls one non-1 failed die</li> <li>Double 9s on the roll and on a success instantly move to close range</li> <li>Add (Essence) bonus dice on the next attack roll, and one automatic success on the damage roll if withering, or a die if decisive.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> And that makes for one crazy badass rush. I mean, Jesus, look at all that.<br /> <br /> Of course you don't then get to use the Water Aura upgrade effects to Water Dragon, but that's what's trying to keep omni-element balanced against single element. You can restrict yourself to the Excellency, Soaring Leap Technique and Crashing Tide Advance and be the Water guy, getting all the Water Aura benefits if you want. You can also be the Avatar who's whirling forward on flaming rocket feet, while bending the roots and trees to grab you and help you along, while blasting yourself from behind with a tempest strength wind. There are benefits to both, one isn't necessarily the automatic winner.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want to give omni-aura as a way of helping to bridge the gap between terrestrial and solar power that might be a good helpful thing to do there, but if you do you should at least be aware that single-element builds no longer have anything making them good compared to mixing them. Your Water Dragon stylist will always benefit from having skin made of stone, flaming rocket feet, and oaken fists. It's not necessarily a bad thing, but it is if your design goal is to allow players to focus on only one element and not be hamstrung.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T16:08:35-07:00","id":1447654,"title":"","content":"That's one turn but it also loses some because of the lack of aura and it's rather expensive. You'll certainly be hitting anima soon after you do that. However, on your bigger point. you can easily refluff things to be one element. Nothing stops that. Instead of skin made of stone, it's covered in fire or water. Instead of flaming rocket feet, it's bursts of wind or being advanced by with vines. Instead of oaken fists it's ice covered fists. You can easily make every charm conform to any of the five elements in one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T17:23:14-07:00","id":1447666,"title":"","content":"You know, the most annoying thing about the second-least fitting Aspect to have Dodge having Dodge is that I have no idea what Ability I\u2019d switch it with. Performance <i>would</i> be a no-brainer except then one Aspect would have all the spoken social.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T17:38:35-07:00","id":1447671,"title":"","content":"You could certainly, but you can refluff anything you like. You could even build a Solar and refluff them as a DB, like Fire and Stones Strike as having actual fire and stones, and Iron Whirlwind being an actual whirlwind and stuff. When you're looking at Aura vs mixed elements you're actually looking at different mechanical effects giving you a unique power depending on what route you take.<br /> <br /> One character can be Aang, and the other Fire Lord Ozai, and they do different things in different ways, but can both be quite powerful. Aang traps an enemy in the ground, then flows around their counterattack like water, and then brings down his fist to drag the air from his lungs. Ozai flashes forward in a streak of fire, ignites a bonfire under his enemy, and then ignites their soul into a pyre. You're making a choice with unique mechanical and fluff differences.<br /> <br /> I think it's interesting, and both approaches have the power to tun anything in Creation into chunky salsa in a split second, so I don't think there's much of a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}